  "description": "Contract-level emergency actions are specified down to the function signature, while the Agent-level and ecosystem-level emergency response protocols that would say who decides, when, and on what evid",
  "orientation": "Contract-level emergency actions are specified down to the function signature, while the Agent-level and ecosystem-level emergency response protocols that would say who decides, when, and on what evidence are almost universally deferred to a future iteration. The result is a system that knows exactly how to execute an emergency and not at all how to declare one \u2014 alongside sweep procedures that cover synchronous positions but not asynchronous ones, whose claim step needs the very Relayer the Freezer may have just removed.",
